============================================================ QUESTION 2
– GIT AND GITHUB
============================================================

AIM

Perform basic Git operations and upload the Student Backend project to
GitHub.

IMPORTANT: Run these commands from the project directory. If the Flask
server is running in another terminal, leave it running or stop it with
Ctrl + C when finished.

STEP 1: Enter the project directory

cd ~/student

STEP 2: Configure Git

Use your own name and the email associated with your GitHub account:

git config –global user.name “YOUR_NAME” git config –global user.email
“YOUR_GITHUB_EMAIL”

Verify:

git config –global –list

STEP 3: Create .gitignore

nano .gitignore

Paste:

venv/ pycache/ *.pyc

Save with Ctrl + O, Enter, Ctrl + X.

STEP 4: Initialize the repository

git init

STEP 5: Check repository status

git status

STEP 6: Add project files

git add .

STEP 7: Check staged files

git status

The venv directory should not be staged because it is listed in
.gitignore.

STEP 8: Commit the files

git commit -m “Student backend application”

STEP 9: Rename the branch to main

git branch -M main

STEP 10: Create a GitHub repository

1.  Open https://github.com/new
2.  Repository name: student-backend (or use your existing repository).
3.  Choose Public or Private as required.
4.  Do not initialize with a README if you are pushing this existing
    local repo.
5.  Click Create repository.

STEP 11: Add the remote repository

For the existing repository used in this practical:

git remote add origin https://github.com/ro-ro48/devops-external1.git

If origin was already added, do not run the command again. Check it
with:

git remote -v

If the URL needs correcting:

git remote set-url origin
https://github.com/ro-ro48/devops-external1.git

STEP 12: Push to GitHub

git push -u origin main

If Git asks for a username, enter your GitHub username.

If Git asks for a password, use a Personal Access Token (PAT), not your
normal GitHub account password. For a classic token, select the repo
scope needed to push to the repository. Keep the token private.

STEP 13: Verify

git log –oneline git remote -v

Open the repository in a browser and confirm that app.py and .gitignore
are visible.

